From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 22:44:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: clear the WED reset completions before a reset

An ethernet reset and the L1 recovery signal each other through two
completions. If one side ends its wait on a timeout, the other side's
late signal stays in its completion. The next reset then does not
wait at all. Clear both completions in the reset callback, before it
publishes the request, so that no signal of that request can be lost.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7915/mmio.c |    4 ++++
 mt7996/mmio.c |    4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7915/mmio.c
+++ b/mt7915/mmio.c
@@ -609,6 +609,10 @@ static int mt7915_mmio_wed_reset(struct
 
 	ASSERT_RTNL();
 
+	/* a signal that came after a timed-out wait must not end this reset */
+	reinit_completion(&mdev->mmio.wed_reset);
+	reinit_completion(&mdev->mmio.wed_reset_complete);
+
 	if (test_and_set_bit(MT76_STATE_WED_RESET, &mphy->state))
 		return -EBUSY;
 
--- a/mt7996/mmio.c
+++ b/mt7996/mmio.c
@@ -515,6 +515,10 @@ static int mt7996_mmio_wed_reset(struct
 
 	ASSERT_RTNL();
 
+	/* a signal that came after a timed-out wait must not end this reset */
+	reinit_completion(&mdev->mmio.wed_reset);
+	reinit_completion(&mdev->mmio.wed_reset_complete);
+
 	if (test_and_set_bit(MT76_STATE_WED_RESET, &mphy->state))
 		return -EBUSY;
 
